{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Init.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Init.Omega"],"declarations":49,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.core_is_three_on_all_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.core_is_three_on_all_three","kind":"theorem","line":442,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L442-L446","doc":"**The core is knot-independent across all three** — the one shared prediction\nof `H_Ad` and `H_floor`, now checked on a third knot rather than two. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.pretzel_is_a_new_data_point","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.pretzel_is_a_new_data_point","kind":"theorem","line":433,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L433-L440","doc":"**The third knot is a genuine extension, not a restatement.** `(−2,3,7)` has a\nremainder of `4`, distinct from both smaller knots — so the arithmetic rule is not\nfitted to a two-point data set. (Its `q→0` Stokes matrix is not published, so this\nis a *prediction*: `R1`/`H_floor` say the `(−2,3,7)` count is `7`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.forced_remainder_is_the_real_embedding_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.forced_remainder_is_the_real_embedding_count","kind":"theorem","line":423,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L423-L431","doc":"**The forced unit remainder of Part 1 is derived, not assumed.** `4₁`'s\nremainder is `0` because its trace field is imaginary quadratic (no real\nembedding); `5₂`'s is `1` because the discriminant `−23` cubic has exactly one.\nThe `+1` that `knot_independent_core_forces_unit_remainder` could only *force* now\nhas an arithmetic source. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.remainder_is_arithmetic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.remainder_is_arithmetic","kind":"theorem","line":416,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L416-L421","doc":"**The remainder equals the count of real embeddings, plus the pairs beyond the\ngeometric one.** For all three knots this is exactly\n`realEmbeddings K + 2·(complexPairs K − 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.floorRemainder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.floorRemainder","kind":"def","line":413,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L413-L414","doc":"The remainder `H_floor` predicts: everything in `P_K` beyond the core. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.floorCore","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.floorCore","kind":"def","line":409,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L409-L411","doc":"`H_floor`'s core: the trivial representation together with one\ncomplex-conjugate pair (the geometric connection and its mirror). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.pk_sizes_three_four_seven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.pk_sizes_three_four_seven","kind":"theorem","line":404,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L404-L407","doc":"**The Garoufalidis–Zagier counts, reproduced from the signatures alone.**\n`|P_K| = 3, 4, 7` for `4₁`, `5₂`, `(−2,3,7)` — matching §2.1 verbatim. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.pkSize","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.pkSize","kind":"def","line":400,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L400-L402","doc":"`|P_K| = 1 + (real embeddings) + 2·(complex pairs)` — the trivial\nrepresentation plus every embedding of the reduced trace algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.complexPairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.complexPairs","kind":"def","line":394,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L394-L398","doc":"Number of **complex-conjugate pairs** of embeddings of `A_K^red`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.realEmbeddings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.realEmbeddings","kind":"def","line":388,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L388-L392","doc":"Number of **real** embeddings of the reduced trace algebra `A_K^red`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.instDecidableEqPKnot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.instDecidableEqPKnot","kind":"instance","line":386,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L386-L386","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.PKnot.pretzel237","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.PKnot.pretzel237","kind":"ctor","line":385,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L385-L385","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.PKnot.fiveTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.PKnot.fiveTwo","kind":"ctor","line":384,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L384-L384","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.PKnot.fourOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.PKnot.fourOne","kind":"ctor","line":383,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L383-L383","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.PKnot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.PKnot","kind":"inductive","line":381,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L381-L386","doc":"The three knots for which Garoufalidis–Zagier tabulate `P_K` (§2.1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.ssyt_weights_nodup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.ssyt_weights_nodup","kind":"theorem","line":330,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L330-L333","doc":"**The grading is multiplicity-free at the tableau level too** — the three\ntableaux carry three distinct weights, matching M2's `sMultiplicities = [1,1,1]`\nwithout adjustment. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.ssyt_meridian_weights_are_twice_adjoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.ssyt_meridian_weights_are_twice_adjoint","kind":"theorem","line":315,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L315-L328","doc":"**The meridian grading is derived, not assumed.** The shape-`(2)` semistandard\ntableaux carry `m`-weights `(2, 0, −2)`, i.e. exactly **twice** the adjoint\n`x`-exponents `(1, 0, −1)` — which is precisely the substitution `x = m²`. So\n`s(x) = x + 1 + x⁻¹` is the character of `S^{(2)}(ℂ²)` in the meridian variable,\nread off Young-tableau combinatorics with nothing fitted.\n\nThis is the discriminator Part 2 asked for: `H_Ad`'s grading variable follows from\nQOU-native Schur–Weyl data, while `H_floor` (whose grading is by Chern–Simons\nvalue) has no route to it. It does **not** by itself decide between them — it\nsupplies `H_Ad` with a mechanism `H_floor` lacks, which is a weaker and different\nthing than excluding `H_floor`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.meridianWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.meridianWeight","kind":"def","line":310,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L310-L313","doc":"The **meridian** weight of a tableau, in exponents of `m`: entry `1` contributes\n`m¹`, entry `2` contributes `m⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.hecke_block_one_schur_partner_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.hecke_block_one_schur_partner_three","kind":"theorem","line":303,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L303-L308","doc":"**The correction, as a theorem.** `dim M_{(2)} = #SYT((2)) = 1` while\n`dim S^{(2)}(ℂ²) = #SSYT((2)) = 3`. The adjoint's `3` is the Schur–Weyl *partner*\nof the `(2)` Hecke block, never the block's own dimension. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.syt_from_strictly_increasing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.syt_from_strictly_increasing","kind":"theorem","line":298,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L298-L301","doc":"**The standard tableaux are exactly the strictly-increasing fillings** — the\n`1` is likewise derived. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.ssyt_from_weakly_increasing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.ssyt_from_weakly_increasing","kind":"theorem","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L293-L296","doc":"**The semistandard tableaux are exactly the weakly-increasing fillings** — the\n`3` is *derived* from the tableau condition, not asserted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.sytShapeTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.sytShapeTwo","kind":"def","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L289-L291","doc":"The standard tableaux of shape `(2)`: each of `1,2` used once, strictly\nincreasing along the row. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.ssytShapeTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.ssytShapeTwo","kind":"def","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L286-L287","doc":"The semistandard tableaux of shape `(2)`: rows weakly increase. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.shapeTwoFillings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.shapeTwoFillings","kind":"def","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L283-L284","doc":"All fillings of the shape-`(2)` row by the alphabet `{1,2}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.palindromic_shape_does_not_arbitrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.palindromic_shape_does_not_arbitrate","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L249-L257","doc":"**Both rivals also fail `T4`'s genericity screen the same way.** `H_floor`'s\nChern–Simons values `{0, +𝔙, −𝔙}` form a 3-element palindromic set exactly as the\nadjoint weights `{1, 0, −1}` do, so the palindromic shape — already known generic —\ncannot arbitrate either. Recorded as the shape identity that makes the point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.h_ad_and_h_floor_are_indistinguishable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.h_ad_and_h_floor_are_indistinguishable","kind":"theorem","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L234-L247","doc":"**`H_Ad` and `H_floor` are observationally indistinguishable on the certified\ndata.** Their cores are equal, so they impose *identical* constraints on any\ncompletion — the same remainder, the same forcing, the same predictions. The\nnumerical agreement `3 = dim 𝔰𝔩₂ = |{0, g, ḡ}|` is therefore not evidence for the\nadjoint reading over the connection-floor reading; only the **grading variable**\n(meridian `x = m²` for `H_Ad`, Chern–Simons value for `H_floor`) could separate them,\nand that separation is not made here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.hyperbolicConnectionFloor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.hyperbolicConnectionFloor","kind":"def","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L229-L232","doc":"The rival hypothesis `H_floor`: the knot-independent core is the triple of flat\nconnections `{0, g, ḡ}` that **every** hyperbolic knot carries — i.e. the universal\nfloor of `R1` itself, with no `𝔰𝔩₂` adjoint anywhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.fourone_is_a_degenerate_observation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.fourone_is_a_degenerate_observation","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L222-L227","doc":"**`4₁` supplies no evidence for `H_Ad` independent of `R1`.** Amphichirality\ncollapses the two projections there (`dtMin = dtMax`), while they genuinely differ at\n`5₂`. So the whole empirical support for \"the core is knot-independently `3`\" is the\n**single** observation `dtMinus 5₂ = 3`: one non-degenerate data point, not two. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.two_scalars_name_what_one_cannot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.two_scalars_name_what_one_cannot","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L209-L218","doc":"**No tension with the scalar-impossibility theorem.**\n`Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.no_scalar_matches_chirality_split_datum` rules out a\n**single** scalar equalling the set-valued `5₂` datum; it says nothing about a\n*pair*. Stated here as the general fact: two scalars suffice to name a 2-element set\nthat neither can name alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.min_max_pair_reconstructs_datum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.min_max_pair_reconstructs_datum","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L202-L207","doc":"**Complementarity: the two projections together reconstruct the datum.** Listing\neach knot's chirality counts in increasing order gives exactly `[dtMin, dtMax]`. So\nthe pair `(H_Ad, R1)` recovers the full set-valued DT datum for both knots. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.h_ad_is_the_dtmin_projection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.h_ad_is_the_dtmin_projection","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L196-L200","doc":"**`H_Ad` is the `dtMin` projection.** The knot-independent adjoint core `s(1)=3`\nequals the *smaller* chirality count on both knots. So `H_Ad` and `R1` are reading\n**different halves** of the same chirality-split datum, not the same half twice. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.r1_is_the_dtmax_projection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.r1_is_the_dtmax_projection","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L191-L194","doc":"**`R1` is the `dtMax` projection.** Route A's surviving reading assigns\n`4₁ ↦ 3`, `5₂ ↦ 4` — precisely the larger chirality count, on both knots. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.dtMax","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.dtMax","kind":"def","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L188-L189","doc":"The larger of the two chirality counts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.dtMin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.dtMin","kind":"def","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L185-L186","doc":"The smaller of the two chirality counts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.dtMinus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.dtMinus","kind":"def","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L179-L183","doc":"The `S⁻` (bar-negative chirality) DT count. Amphichirality forces\n`dtMinus 4₁ = dtPlus 4₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.dtPlus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.dtPlus","kind":"def","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L174-L177","doc":"The `S⁺` (bar-positive chirality) DT count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.no_purely_knot_independent_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.no_purely_knot_independent_count","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L154-L161","doc":"**The falsifier, stated as a theorem.** If some completion claims the count is\n*purely* knot-independent (no remainder at all), it contradicts the certified\nsplit. So `H_Ad` alone is provably incomplete — it is not a candidate for the\nwhole answer, and saying so is not a concession but a derived fact. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.adjoint_core_pins_remainder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.adjoint_core_pins_remainder","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L142-L152","doc":"**Under `H_Ad` the remainder is pinned to `0` and `1`.** Taking the\nknot-independent core to be the adjoint count `s(1) = 3`, the `4₁` remainder\nvanishes and the `5₂` remainder is exactly one state. Any completion of `H_Ad`\nmust derive that single extra `5₂` ray independently — it cannot be assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.knot_independent_core_forces_unit_remainder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.knot_independent_core_forces_unit_remainder","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L130-L140","doc":"**A knot-independent core forces a knot-dependent remainder differing by one.**\nIf a count decomposes as a constant `core` plus a per-knot `extra`, and reproduces\nthe certified `(3, 4)` split, then `extra` is larger at `5₂` by exactly `1` —\nwhatever the core is. The \"extra state for `5₂`\" is therefore not an optional\npatch: it is forced, with a definite value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.instDecidableEqKKnot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.instDecidableEqKKnot","kind":"instance","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L126-L126","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.KKnot.fiveTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.KKnot.fiveTwo","kind":"ctor","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L125-L125","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.KKnot.fourOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.KKnot.fourOne","kind":"ctor","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L124-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.KKnot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.KKnot","kind":"inductive","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L122-L126","doc":"The two knots carrying certified DT data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.s_at_one_eq_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.s_at_one_eq_three","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L113-L114","doc":"**`s(1) = 3 = dim 𝔰𝔩₂`**, matching M2's `sAtOne`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.sAtOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.sAtOne","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L108-L111","doc":"The character value at the parabolic point `x = 1` is the number of weights:\n`s(1) = 3`. (Each weight contributes `1` because the weights are\nmultiplicity-free.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.adjoint_palindromic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.adjoint_palindromic","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L102-L106","doc":"**The weight set is closed under negation** (`x ↔ x⁻¹`), i.e. the index set is\nbar-symmetric — the same `q ↦ q⁻¹` involution that grades the DT split in\n`ChiralityGradedCount`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.adjoint_dim_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.adjoint_dim_three","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L99-L100","doc":"**`dim 𝔰𝔩₂ = 3`** — the number of adjoint weights. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.adjoint_multiplicity_free","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.adjoint_multiplicity_free","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L95-L97","doc":"**Multiplicity-free**: the adjoint weights are pairwise distinct, matching\nM2's `sMultiplicities = [1,1,1]` with no adjustment. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.adjointExponents","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.AdjointIndexSetM3.adjointExponents","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/AdjointIndexSetM3.lean#L91-L93","doc":"The `x`-exponents of the adjoint representation of `𝔰𝔩₂`, i.e. the weights\n`{2, 0, −2}` written in the variable `x = m²`: `(x, 1, x⁻¹) ↦ (1, 0, −1)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}